.TH EUCLID-CLI-ETS-DELETE-SERVER 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ets-delete-server \- delete a transfer server definition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ets delete-server
.BR \-\-server\-id | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a transfer server definition.
.PP
A server that is currently running is stopped: the Euclid manager runs
exactly the servers that are defined and marked running, so a definition
that no longer exists is torn down on its next reconcile pass, a few
seconds later. Clients connected at that moment are disconnected.
.PP
Nothing in the bucket is touched. The objects clients uploaded through
this server remain, and are still reachable through
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1)
or any other transfer server pointed at the same bucket. Deleting a
server removes an access route, not the data behind it.
.PP
The definition itself is not recoverable - there is no undo, and
recreating the server means passing every setting again. To take a
server out of service temporarily, use
.BR euclid-cli-ets-stop-server (1)
instead, which keeps the definition.
.PP
An SFTP server's host key file is left on disk. Recreating a server with
the same
.B \-\-host\-key
path therefore keeps its old identity, and clients that pinned it
continue to connect without complaint.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-server\-id " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the server to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The definition was deleted; the server ID is printed as JSON with
\fIdeleted\fR \fItrue\fR.
.TP
.B 1
Missing or invalid arguments, the caller is not an authenticated
administrator, the server could not be reached, or no server has that ID
(HTTP 404).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets delete-server \e
    --server-id sftp1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check what a server is before removing it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets get-server \e
    --server-id sftp1
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets delete-server \e
    --server-id sftp1
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ets (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-stop-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-create-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-get-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-objects (1)
